WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.670
Japan sits on the Ring of Fire,
where several tectonic plates meet.

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.630
It has roughly a tenth of
all the world's earthquakes,

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.570
and 111 active volcanoes.

4
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:15.770
Typhoons, torrential rain
and heavy snow strike too.

5
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.950
Yet 123.8 million people live there.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.770
So how do so many people
live with so many hazards?

7
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.210
In this mission, you'll learn four
ways people live with hazards,

8
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.230
and find a Japanese example of each.

9
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.890
Then you'll weigh how well
Japan's responses work,

10
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.350
and where they fall short.

11
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:41.330
Your mission: explain how more than 120
million people live with Japan's hazards.
